 phase mixing and the resonant absorption of the mhd alfvn waves @xcite , the instability caused by the warm proton beams or by the ion - ion streaming @xcite , the velocity shear transition @xcite , and the parametric decay by other wave modes @xcite . these wave generation mechanisms make it easily to produce the opposite traveling mhd alfvn wave and kaw , thus causing the nonlocal interaction . the mechanism proposed in this study is also different from the other two kinds of interactions among three alfvn waves , the local interaction and the nonlocal decay @xcite . the proposed wave - wave interaction happens for alfvn waves with different scales , whereas the local interaction is limited to waves with comparable scales @xcite . the nonlocal decay mechanism also relates to three waves with different scales , however , it describes two waves excited by a pump wave @xcite . of course , two nonlocal interactions , either through the nonlocal decay or through our nonlocal interaction , can both directly transport the alfvn wave energy from the large - scale region to the small - scale region and then dissipate the wave energy there . last , let us give a simple discussion for a potential application of our nonlocal mechanism . recent observations showed there exists the kaw even down to the electron scales ( the electron inertial length or the electron gyroradius scale ) in the solar wind @xcite . this electron scale kaw can not be explained by the local wave cascade mechanism because the large electron landau damping can totally dissipate the kaw energy in that small scale region @xcite . but our results implies , except for the local wave - wave interaction , the nonlocal wave - wave interaction may also happen in the alfvn wave turbulence . furthermore , as shown in figure 2 , the nonlocal coupling is stronger for the smaller scale kaws . so the observed electron scale kaws may be produced by this nonlocal mechanism . it should be pointed out that the nonlocal turbulence of the kaws still receives little attention and this problem will be further investigated in our future works . this paper discusses the nonlocal coupling of one mhd alfvn wave and two kaws , a mhd alfvn wave + kaw 1 @xmath0 kaw 2 . the qualitative discussion shows that this wave - wave interaction works in the plasmas with @xmath33 . the frequency relations among the two kaws and the mhd alfvn wave are @xmath34 and @xmath35 . the quantitative discussion shows that the coupling is stronger for the more obliquely propagating mhd alfvn wave and for the kaws with lager perpendicular wavenumbers . we also show that the proposed mechanism may play an important role in generating electron scale kaws in the solar wind . the authors acknowledge referees for their assistances in evaluating the manuscript . this study has been supported by the nsfc grants 10973043 , 40874087 , 41074107 and 41031063 , the nkbrsf under 2011cb81102 , the cma grant gyhy201106011 , and the cas special grant for postgraduate research , innovation and practice . financial support by ocean public welfare scientific research project , state oceanic administration people s republic of china ( no.201005017 ) is also acknowledged . d. j. wu and y. yang , astron . astrophys . * 452 * , l7 ( 2006 ) . d. j. wu and y. yang , astrophys . j. * 659 * , 1693 ( 2007 ) . p. louarn , j .- e . wahlund , t. chust , h. de feraudy , a. roux , b. holback , p. o. dovner , a. i. eriksson and g. holmgren , geophys . * 21 * , 1847 ( 1994 ) . d. j. wu , g. l. huang and d. y. wang , phys . rev . lett . * 77 * , 4346 ( 1996 ) . c. chaston , c. w. carlson , w. j. peria , r. e. ergun and j. p. mcfadden , geophys . * 26 * , 647 ( 1999 ) . w. gekelman , j. geophys . res . * 104 * , 14417 ( 1999 ) . d. leneman , w. gekelman , and j. maggs , phys . 82 * , 2673 ( 1999 ) . c. a. kletzing , s. r. bounds , j. martin - hiner , w. gekelman and c. mitchell , phys . lett . * 90 * , 035004 ( 2003 ) . s. vincena , w. gekelman , and 